        "original_id": "65ec59ef-2522-54e5-adc0-0a7b32a36aa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Double\n- Products: Blue, \"Woman of the World\", \"Rangoon Moon\", \"The Captain of Her Heart\"\n- Places: Europe\n- Topics: Swiss music duo, hit singles\n\nFacts:\n- Double was a Swiss music duo pronounced \"doo-blay\".\n- Blue included updated versions of Double's earlier singles \"Woman of the World\" and \"Rangoon Moon\".\n- \"The Captain of Her Heart\" was included on Blue.\n- \"The Captain of Her Heart\" was a plaintive, atmospheric, piano-led ballad.\n- \"The Captain of Her Heart\" was released as a single in 1986 and became an immediate success throughout Europe.\n- Double was best known for the hit single \"The Captain of Her Heart\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ae02cc56-21cd-5a27-87f5-05144677935c",
        "text": "Page: Blue (Double album). Sentence: In addition to containing updated versions of two of the band's earlier singles (\"Woman of the World\" and \"Rangoon Moon\"), the album included the international smash hit, \"The Captain of Her Heart\", a plaintive, atmospheric, piano-led ballad which was an immediate success throughout Europe upon its 1986 single release.\nPage: Double (band). Sentence: Double (pronounced \"doo-blay\") was a Swiss music duo best known for their hit single \"The Captain of Her Heart\".",
